# The Fusion route to modelPath in Resolve Studio 21.2.0.5, 2026-11-26.
#
# Question: the scripted OFX effect object has no SetParam - only GetInfo,
# GetIndex, GetIsEnabled, SetIndex and SetIsEnabled - but it does offer
# GetFusionComp. Can modelPath be set through the effect's Fusion comp, so the
# frame stops being a pass-through and onnxruntime_providers_cuda loads?
#
# Answer: no. GetFusionComp() returns None for an effect added with
# AddEffect("ofx", ...), and a Fusion comp added to the timeline item does not
# take the OFX node either. Both shapes were tried in one session each.

## 0. what was installed and rendered

bundle: templates/onnx-inference-ofx/build/bundle/OnnxInference.ofx.bundle, built
against the 1.20.1 GPU package (ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT=.validation/ort-gpu-1.20.1,
OFXPLUGIN_BUNDLE_CUDA_PROVIDER=ON), so the cuBLAS-12 imports resolve in this host
onnxruntime_providers_cuda.dll: 673,741,344 bytes
onnxruntime-ofx.dll: 12,400,160 bytes
installed into: C:\Program Files\Common Files\OFX\Plugins\OnnxInference.ofx.bundle
source: .validation/resolve-source.png, 1920x1080
model: templates/onnx-inference-ofx/models/test_conv.onnx

