## 3. what the module list says about the host, not about the plug-in

`tasklist /FI "IMAGENAME eq Resolve.exe" /M` lists onnxruntime.dll in the host
before the plug-in has run a session at all: Resolve ships its own ONNX Runtime.
A module-name check therefore cannot show which runtime answered - the bundled
core is called onnxruntime-ofx.dll for exactly that reason - and
onnxruntime_providers_cuda was not loaded in either run, because no session was
created without modelPath.

## 4. conclusion

modelPath cannot be reached in this host through either Fusion shape. What remains
is a project that already carries the value (a .drp written with the parameter
set) or a host whose effect object exposes a parameter API. Until one of those
exists, the frame stays a pass-through and the claim that the plug-in uses
Resolve's own cuDNN stays unproven.
